WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.003
OMERTÀ connects a persistent crime game to an on-chain economy.

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:08.407
Players build characters, earn cash, spend OMR, and compete over property.

00:00:08.407 --> 00:00:12.010
This film explains the current launch design and implementation.

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:17.215
Production trading, staking rewards, NFT issuance, and stock delivery still require launch approval.

00:00:18.333 --> 00:00:22.343
Inside the city, cash pays for equipment, operations, and survival.

00:00:22.343 --> 00:00:24.749
OMR powers premium actions and commitments.

00:00:24.749 --> 00:00:26.353
Cash never buys OMR.

00:00:26.353 --> 00:00:29.962
ETH enters through supported market trades and paid services.

00:00:29.962 --> 00:00:34.373
Spending OMR recycles inventory; moving game balances on-chain requires verified backing.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:39.505
OMR has a fixed supply of one hundred million tokens.

00:00:39.505 --> 00:00:43.110
Trading, gameplay accounting, and inventory programs move existing value.

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:45.514
They do not create extra tokens.

00:00:45.514 --> 00:00:48.317
The launch plan auctions sixty million OMR.

00:00:48.317 --> 00:00:52.323
Total supply, circulating supply, and treasury inventory are different quantities.

00:00:53.433 --> 00:00:56.235
The base protocol fee is four percent.

00:00:56.235 --> 00:01:04.639
It splits across operations, the stock acquisition recipient, community, protocol liquidity, and ETH staking rewards, in the exact percentages shown here.

00:01:04.639 --> 00:01:08.241
Opening or sell surge can add half a percent.

00:01:08.241 --> 00:01:10.242
Liquidity provider fees are separate.

00:01:10.242 --> 00:01:14.645
Family turf can direct eligible future liquidity fees, never liquidity principal.

00:01:15.767 --> 00:01:19.768
On-chain OMR staking earns a share of ETH actually funded.

00:01:19.768 --> 00:01:23.369
Every deposit has its own thirty-day minimum withdrawal lock.

00:01:23.369 --> 00:01:25.770
Matured principal keeps earning until withdrawn.

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:29.371
Earned claims and mature exits remain available during pauses.

00:01:29.371 --> 00:01:32.172
There is no promised fixed annual return.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:42.112
The city contains twenty-five hundred permanent Street Deeds: one thousand earned through gameplay, one thousand paid mints, and five hundred partnership properties.

00:01:42.112 --> 00:01:44.515
Earned discovery begins at level twenty-five.

00:01:44.515 --> 00:01:51.324
Both public routes create the same type of property, with the same operating rules and loss risks.

00:01:52.433 --> 00:01:55.237
Your soulbound identity NFT represents the bloodline.

00:01:55.237 --> 00:01:59.243
A separate escrow holds equipped Deeds for each mortal life.

00:01:59.243 --> 00:02:06.052
Equipped Deeds and their stock assets can pass to a player killer after recorded death and settlement.

00:02:06.052 --> 00:02:08.455
Safe release needs twenty-four hours' notice.

00:02:08.455 --> 00:02:14.063
Other deaths send inheritance to the exact heir after a separate twenty-four-hour estate delay.

00:02:15.167 --> 00:02:18.368
Stocks belong in the Deed's own token-bound account.

00:02:18.368 --> 00:02:24.771
New rewards require equipment on a living character, no pending exit, Broker activation, and qualifying play.

00:02:24.771 --> 00:02:31.575
Three activity tracks and a score of twenty-five determine eligibility for a proportional share of acquired stock.

00:02:31.575 --> 00:02:35.176
Purchases and deliveries require funded assets and enabled settlement.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:41.107
The backend records authoritative gameplay; EVM contracts enforce on-chain custody and settlement.

00:02:41.107 --> 00:02:47.515
Node and Fastify serve the game, PostgreSQL stores its state, and viem connects wallets and contracts.

00:02:47.515 --> 00:02:50.319
Keepers connect confirmed game events with contracts.

00:02:50.319 --> 00:02:53.123
Dashboards must reflect the state actually observed.

00:02:54.233 --> 00:02:56.236
Implementation is different from activation.

00:02:56.236 --> 00:03:03.045
Current records show production database preparation and partnership reservations, but no contract deployment or minted partnership NFTs.

00:03:03.045 --> 00:03:07.051
Funding, verified configuration, indexing, and owner approval remain launch gates.

00:03:07.051 --> 00:03:11.056
Treat every reward flow as conditional until those gates open.
